<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rohingya</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rohingya people</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rohingya are a mainly Muslim people of Rakhine State in western Myanmar, close to the border with Bangladesh. Myanmar's 1982 citizenship law left most of them stateless, and they have faced repeated persecution. In 2017 army 'clearance operations' drove over 700,000 of them into Bangladesh, where they live in large refugee camps, and the violence has been examined by international courts as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">genocide</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rohingya.jpg" alt="Rohingya" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rohingya Language Academy SVG versionː MS Sakib · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rohingya_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
